# AgentQ -- byte-exactness rules.
#
# The project's hard constraint is that assets/unix/agentq-server and
# assets/windows-git-bash/agentq are byte-identical (run-tests.sh check 01
# asserts `cmp` returns 0).  Line-ending translation would break that, and it
# would break it silently on a machine whose core.autocrlf is not `false` --
# which is the common case on Windows, where these assets are actually used.
#
# So: never translate.  Every file is stored and checked out exactly as it is.
# `-text` also stops git from treating any file as text for diff/merge
# purposes, which is what we want for assets that must not be rewritten.
* -text

# Shell and PowerShell sources keep their own line endings verbatim.
*.sh   -text
*.bash -text
*.ps1  -text
*.cmd  -text

# The two canonical server copies: explicitly binary, so no filter can ever
# touch them even if a future .gitattributes adds one.
assets/unix/agentq-server          -text -diff
assets/windows-git-bash/agentq     -text -diff
